{"abstract":"The paper presents a method to operationalize Jan Gehl’s questions for public space into metrics to map Russian monotowns’ urban life in 2017. With the use of social media data, it becomes possible to scale Gehl’s approach from the survey of small urban areas to the analysis of entire cities while maintaining the human scale’s resolution. When underperforming public spaces are detected, we propose a matrix for urban design interventions using Jane Jacobs’ typologies for good city life. Furthermore, this method could be deployed to improve the conditions of public spaces in Russian monotowns through a series of architectural briefs for design competitions and urban design guidelines for local administrations.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Cerrone, Damiano","Baeza, Jesus Lopez","Lehtovuori, Panu","Quercia, Daniele","Schifanella, Rossano","Aiello, Luca Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383956"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","HafenCity University Hamburg","Nokia Bell Labs","Tampere University","University of Turin"],"keyword":["G I S","Urban analytics","dataviz","monotowns"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implementing gehl s theory to study urban space the case of monotowns","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su13095105","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383956","identifier":[{"id":"85105661794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b821ac00-221b-4023-aaf5-570cdcb412a7"],"keyword":["G.I.S","dataviz","monotowns","urban analytics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-276BCBC985AAFAB1364322247F42AD42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426569/sustainability21ghel.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su13095105","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"tampere university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Tampere University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"hafencity university hamburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"HafenCity University Hamburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of turin","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Turin","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Damiano","key":"cerronepau","last":"Cerrone","name":"Cerrone, Damiano","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesus Lopez","key":"baezapau","last":"Baeza","name":"Baeza, Jesus Lopez","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Panu","key":"lehtovuoripau","last":"Lehtovuori","name":"Lehtovuori, Panu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rossano","key":"schifanellapau","last":"Schifanella","name":"Schifanella, Rossano","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/su13095105","issn":["20711050"],"issue":"9","journal":"Sustainability","paperid":"5105","publisher":"MDPI AG","status":"p","title":"Sustainability","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105661794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b821ac00-221b-4023-aaf5-570cdcb412a7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Implementing Gehl’s Theory to Study Urban Space. The Case of Monotowns","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383956","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Since the uptake of social media, researchers have mined online discussions to track the outbreak and evolution of specific diseases or chronic conditions such as influenza or depression. To broaden the set of diseases under study, we developed a Deep Learning tool for Natural Language Processing that extracts mentions of virtually any medical condition or disease from unstructured social media text. With that tool at hand, we processed Reddit and Twitter posts, analyzed the clusters of the two resulting co-occurrence networks of conditions, and discovered that they correspond to well-defined categories of medical conditions. This resulted in the creation of the first comprehensive taxonomy of medical conditions automatically derived from online discussions. We validated the structure of our taxonomy against the official International Statistical Classification of Diseases and Related Health Problems (ICD-11), finding matches of our clusters with 20 official categories, out of 22. Based on the mentions of our taxonomy's sub-categories on Reddit posts geo-referenced in the U.S., we were then able to compute disease-specific health scores. As opposed to counts of disease mentions or counts with no knowledge of our taxonomy's structure, we found that our disease-specific health scores are causally linked with the officially reported prevalences of 18 conditions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scepanovic, Sanja","Aiello, Luca Maria","Zhou, Ke","Quercia, Daniele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383183"],"event":{"acronym":"ICWSM","title":"International AAAI Conference on Web and Social Media"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nokia Bell Labs"],"keyword":["Deep learning","Disease surveillance","Medical Taxonomy","Natural Language Processing","Social Media Mining"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the healthy states of america creating a health taxonomy with social media","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/ICWSM/article/view/18089/17892","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383183","ids":["itu-8248a361-6273-4941-af33-e6af9730f1bc"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Disease Surveillance","Medical Taxonomy","Natural Language Processing","Social Media Mining"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-44805BF2ED7153EF258B388231480572"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/ICWSM/article/view/18089/17892","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426620/icwsm21healthy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanja","key":"scepanovicpau","last":"Scepanovic","name":"Scepanovic, Sanja","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Ke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","pages":"621-632","publisher":"AAAI Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Fifteenth International AAAI Conference on Web and Social Media","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8248a361-6273-4941-af33-e6af9730f1bc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Healthy States of America: Creating a Health Taxonomy with Social Media","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383183","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Quantifying a society’s value system is important because it suggests what people deeply care about—it reflects who they actually are and, more importantly, who they will like to be. This cultural quantification has been typically done by studying literary production. However, a society’s value system might well be implicitly quantified based on the decisions that people took in the past and that were mediated by what they care about. It turns out that one class of these decisions is visible in ordinary settings: it is visible in street names. We studied the names of 4,932 honorific streets in the cities of Paris, Vienna, London and New York. We chose these four cities because they were important centers of cultural influence for the Western world in the 20th century. We found that street names greatly reflect the extent to which a society is gender biased, which professions are considered elite ones, and the extent to which a city is influenced by the rest of the world. This way of quantifying a society’s value system promises to inform new methodologies in Digital Humanities; makes it possible for municipalities to reflect on their past to inform their future; and informs the design of everyday’s educational tools that promote historical awareness in a playful way.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Banchilon, Melanie","Constantinides, Marios","Bogucka, Edyta","Aiello, Luca Maria","Quercia, Daniele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381818"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nokia Bell Labs","Technical University of Munich","Washington University in St. Louis"],"keyword":["Culture","Urban informatics","Wikipedia","steet names"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"streetonomics quantifying culture using street names","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0252869","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381818","identifier":[{"id":"85108950079","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-24cc0a7c-3c44-497d-87d6-f927ac22e359"],"keyword":["culture","steet names","urban informatics","wikipedia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-91573F75459C8B75B246FF7C61D8F20A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426532/output.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0252869","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"washington university in st louis","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Washington University in St. Louis","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"banchilonpau","last":"Banchilon","name":"Banchilon, Melanie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marios","key":"constantinidespau","last":"Constantinides","name":"Constantinides, Marios","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Edyta","key":"boguckapau","last":"Bogucka","name":"Bogucka, Edyta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0252869","issn":["19326203"],"journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0252869","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108950079"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-24cc0a7c-3c44-497d-87d6-f927ac22e359"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Streetonomics: Quantifying culture using street names","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381818","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction A hypercoagulable condition was described in patients with coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) and proposed as a possible pathogenic mechanism contributing to disease progression and lethality. Aim We evaluated if in-hospital administration of heparin improved survival in a large cohort of Italian COVID-19 patients. Methods In a retrospective observational study, 2,574 unselected patients hospitalized in 30 clinical centers in Italy from February 19, 2020 to June 5, 2020 with laboratory-confirmed severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus-2 infection were analyzed. The primary endpoint in a time-to event analysis was in-hospital death, comparing patients who received heparin (low-molecular-weight heparin [LMWH] or unfractionated heparin [UFH]) with patients who did not. We used multivariable Cox proportional-hazards regression models with inverse probability for treatment weighting by propensity scores. Results Out of 2,574 COVID-19 patients, 70.1% received heparin. LMWH was largely the most used formulation (99.5%). Death rates for patients receiving heparin or not were 7.4 and 14.0 per 1,000 person-days, respectively. After adjustment for propensity scores, we found a 40% lower risk of death in patients receiving heparin (hazard ratio = 0.60; 95% confidence interval: 0.49-0.74; E-value = 2.04). This association was particularly evident in patients with a higher severity of disease or strong coagulation activation. Conclusion In-hospital heparin treatment was associated with a lower mortality, particularly in severely ill COVID-19 patients and in those with strong coagulation activation. The results from randomized clinical trials are eagerly awaited to provide clear-cut recommendations.","author_count":103,"contributors":["Di Castelnuovo, Augusto","Costanzo, Simona","Antinori, Andrea","Berselli, Nausicaa","Blandi, Lorenzo","Bonaccio, Marialaura","Cauda, Roberto","Guaraldi, Giovanni","Menicanti, Lorenzo","Mennuni, Marco","Parruti, Giustino","Patti, Giuseppe","Santilli, Francesca","Signorelli, Carlo","Vergori, Alessandra","Abete, Pasquale","Ageno, Walter","Agodi, Antonella","Agostoni, Piergiuseppe","Aiello, Luca","Al Moghazi, Samir","Arboretti, Rosa","Astuto, Marinella","Aucella, Filippo","Barbieri, Greta","Bartoloni, Alessandro","Bonfanti, Paolo","Cacciatore, Francesco","Caiano, Lucia","Carrozzi, Laura","Cascio, Antonio","Ciccullo, Arturo","Cingolani, Antonella","Cipollone, Francesco","Colomba, Claudia","Colombo, Crizia","Crosta, Francesca","Danzi, Gian Battista","D'Ardes, Damiano","De Gaetano Donati, Katleen","Di Gennaro, Francesco","Di Tano, Giuseppe","D'Offizi, Gianpiero","Fantoni, Massimo","Fusco, Francesco Maria","Gentile, Ivan","Gianfagna, Francesco","Grandone, Elvira","Graziani, Emauele","Grisafi, Leonardo","Guarnieri, Gabriella","Larizza, Giovanni","Leone, Armando","MacCagni, Gloria","Madaro, Ferruccio","Maitan, Stefano","Mancarella, Sandro","Mapelli, Massimo","Maragna, Riccardo","Marcucci, Rossella","Maresca, Giulio","Marongiu, Silvia","Marotta, Claudia","Marra, Lorenzo","Mastroianni, Franco","Mazzitelli, Maria","Mengozzi, Alessandro","Menichetti, Francesco","Meschiari, Marianna","Milic, Jovana","Minutolo, Filippo","Molena, Beatrice","Montineri, Arturo","Mussini, Cristina","Musso, Maria","Niola, Daniela","Odone, Anna","Olivieri, Marco","Palimodde, Antonella","Parisi, Roberta","Pasi, Emanuela","Pesavento, Raffaele","Petri, Francesco","Pinchera, Biagio","Poletti, Venerino","Ravaglia, Claudia","Rognoni, Andrea","Rossato, Marco","Rossi, Marianna","Sangiovanni, Vincenzo","Sanrocco, Carlo","Scorzolini, Laura","Sgariglia, Raffaella","Simeone, Paola Giustina","Taddei, Eleonora","Torti, Carlo","Vettor, Roberto","Vianello, Andrea","Vinceti, Marco","Virano, Alexandra","Vocciante, Laura","De Caterina, Raffaele","Iacoviello, Licia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259438"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Eur