{"abstract":"Empathy is the tendency to understand and share others' thoughts and feelings. Literature in psychology has shown through surveys potential beneficial implications of empathy. Prior psychology literature showed that a particular type of empathy called \"situational empathy\" --- an immediate empathic response to a triggering situation (e.g., a distressing situation) --- is reflected in the language people use in response to the situation. However, this has not so far been properly measured at scale. In this work, we collected 4k textual reactions (and corresponding situational empathy labels) to different stories. Driven by theoretical concepts, we developed computational models to predict situational empathy from text and, in so doing, we built and made available a list of empathy-related words. When applied to Reddit posts and movie transcripts, our models produced results that matched prior theoretical findings, offering evidence of external validity and suggesting its applicability to unstructured data. The capability of measuring proxies for empathy at scale might benefit a variety of areas such as social media, digital healthcare, and workplace well-being.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhou, Ke","Aiello, Luca Maria","Scepanovic, Sanja","Quercia, Daniele","Konrath, Sarah"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383568"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","title":"ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Indiana University","Nokia Bell Labs"],"keyword":["Computational modeling","Empathy","Natural Language Processing NLP","Situational Empathy","Text analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the language of situational empathy","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426635/cscw21empathy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383568","identifier":[{"id":"85102061894","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9da90335-1f5d-43b1-8f7a-ea7a424906eb"],"keyword":["Computational Modeling","Empathy","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Situational Empathy","Text Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7AFA7E2F3D2190A65DBDB2B2719DC6B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426635/cscw21empathy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"indiana university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Indiana University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Ke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanja","key":"scepanovicpau","last":"Scepanovic","name":"Scepanovic, Sanja","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"konrathpau","last":"Konrath","name":"Konrath, Sarah","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3449087","edition":"1","pages":"1-19","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102061894"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9da90335-1f5d-43b1-8f7a-ea7a424906eb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Language of Situational Empathy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383568","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Disruptions resulting from an epidemic might often appear to amount to chaos but, in reality, can be understood in a systematic way through the lens of “epidemic psychology”. According to Philip Strong, the founder of the sociological study of epidemic infectious diseases, not only is an epidemic biological; there is also the potential for three psycho-social epidemics: of fear, moralization, and action. This work empirically tests Strong’s model at scale by studying the use of language of 122M tweets related to the COVID-19 pandemic posted in the U.S. during the whole year of 2020. On Twitter, we identified three distinct phases. Each of them is characterized by different regimes of the three psycho-social epidemics. In the refusal phase, users refused to accept reality despite the increasing number of deaths in other countries. In the anger phase (started after the announcement of the first death in the country), users’ fear translated into anger about the looming feeling that things were about to change. Finally, in the acceptance phase, which began after the authorities imposed physical-distancing measures, users settled into a “new normal” for their daily activities. Overall, refusal of accepting reality gradually died off as the year went on, while acceptance increasingly took hold. During 2020, as cases surged in waves, so did anger, re-emerging cyclically at each wave. Our real-time operationalization of Strong’s model is designed in a way that makes it possible to embed epidemic psychology into real-time models (e.g., epidemiological and mobility models).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aiello, Luca Maria","Quercia, Daniele","Zhou, Ke","Constantinides, Marios","Scepanovic, Sanja","Joglekar, Sagar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384986"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nokia Bell Labs"],"keyword":["Covid 19","Twitter","epidemic psychology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how epidemic psychology works on twitter evolution of responses to the covid 000000000019 pandemic in the u s","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1057/s41599-021-00861-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384986","identifier":[{"id":"85111085794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fd20ae8f-3b79-49b3-bc42-dab8d13bd06e"],"keyword":["covid-19","epidemic psychology","twitter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-573E8805625366A606E4E38F5AF4F9AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426492/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1057/s41599-021-00861-3","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Ke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marios","key":"constantinidespau","last":"Constantinides","name":"Constantinides, Marios","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanja","key":"scepanovicpau","last":"Scepanovic","name":"Scepanovic, Sanja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sagar","key":"joglekarpau","last":"Joglekar","name":"Joglekar, Sagar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1057/s41599-021-00861-3","issn":["20551045"],"journal":"Humanities and social sciences communications","pages":"1-15","paperid":"179","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"Humanities and social sciences communications","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111085794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fd20ae8f-3b79-49b3-bc42-dab8d13bd06e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How epidemic psychology works on Twitter: evolution of responses to the COVID-19 pandemic in the U.S.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384986","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Sleep scientists have extensively validated the continuity hypothesis, according to which our dreams reflect what happens during our waking life. Yet, only a few attempts have been made to increase the general public’s awareness about the benefits of dream analysis in better understanding and improving our daily life. We designed “The Dreamcatcher,” an interactive visual tool that explores the link between dreams and waking life through a collection of dream reports. We conducted a user study with 154 participants and found a 25% increase in the number of people believing that dream analysis can improve our daily lives after interacting with our tool. The visualization informed people about the potential of the continuity hypothesis to a surprising extent, to the point that it increased their concerns about sharing their own dream reports, thus opening new questions on how to design privacy-aware tools for dream collection.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bogucka, Edyta","Aseniero, Bon Adriel","Aiello, Luca Maria","Quercia, Daniele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383359"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Autodesk Inc","Nokia Bell Labs","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Pattern analysis","Privacy","Sleep","Solid modeling","Visualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the dreamcatcher interactive storytelling of dreams","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426595/output.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383359","identifier":[{"id":"85105598339","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8e3bb6cf-06c3-41a4-b2a3-367fb8d33b0e"],"keyword":["Pattern analysis","Privacy","Sleep","Solid modeling","Visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A6F1D788EF794C97996C7ACE0CD25F5B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426595/output.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"autodesk inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Autodesk Inc","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Edyta","key":"boguckapau","last":"Bogucka","name":"Bogucka, Edyta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bon Adriel","key":"asenieropau","last":"Aseniero","name":"Aseniero, Bon Adriel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mcg.2021.3068794","issn":["02721716","15581756"],"issn_org":["02721716"],"journal":"IEEE Computer Graphics and Applications","pages":"105-112","paperid":"33961549","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Computer Graphics and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105598339"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8e3bb6cf-06c3-41a4-b2a3-367fb8d33b0e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Dreamcatcher: Interactive Storytelling of Dreams","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383359","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Non Fungible Tokens (NFTs) are digital assets that represent objects like art, collectible, and in-game items. They are traded online, often with cryptocurrency, and are generally encoded within smart contracts on a blockchain. Public attention towards NFTs has exploded in 2021, when their market has experienced record sales, but little is known about the overall structure and evolution of its market. Here, we analyse data concerning 6.1 million trades of 4.7 million NFTs between June 23, 2017 and April 27, 2021, obtained primarily from Ethereum and WAX blockchains. First, we characterize statistical properties of the market. Second, we build the network of interactions, show that traders typically specialize on NFTs associated with similar objects and form tight clusters with other traders that exchange the same kind of objects. Third, we cluster objects associated to NFTs according to their visual features and show that collections contain visually homogeneous objects. Finally, we investigate the predictability of NFT sales using simple machine learning algorithms and find that sale history and, secondarily, visual features are good predictors for price. We anticipate that these findings will stimulate further research on NFT production, adoption, and trading in different contexts.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nadini, Matthieu","Alessandretti, Laura","Di Giacinto, Flavio","Martino, Mauro","Aiello, Luca Maria","Baronchelli, Andrea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384517"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","City, University of London","IBM Research"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Cryptocurrency","Digital Assets","Ethereum Blockchain","Machine Learning Predictions","NFT Market Analysis","Non Fungible Tokens","Smart contracts","Trade networks","Visual Features","WAX Blockchain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mapping the nft revolution market trends trade networks and visual features","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-021-00053-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384517","identifier":[{"id":"85117695753","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-dcefcc09-d77e-4b63-8f9e-7283743f8f24"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Cryptocurrency","Digital Assets","Ethereum Blockchain","Machine Learning Predictions","NFT Market Analysis","Non-Fungible Tokens","Smart Contracts","Trade Networks","Visual Features","WAX Blockchain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2F354B471CEF420C57AD330484C1AB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86426704/2106.00647.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-021-00053-8","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"city university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City, University of London","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"catholic university of the sacred heart","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Catholic University of the Sacred Heart","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"ibm research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"IBM Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthieu","key":"nadinipau","last":"Nadini","name":"Nadini, Matthieu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"alessandrettipau","last":"Alessandretti","name":"Alessandretti, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Flavio","key":"digiacintopau","last":"Di Giacinto","name":"Di Giacinto, Flavio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mauro","key":"martinopau","last":"Martino","name":"Martino, Mauro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"baronchellipau","last":"Baronchelli","name":"Baronchelli, Andrea","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117695753"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-dcefcc09-d77e-4b63-8f9e-7283743f8f24"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mapping the NFT revolution: market trends, trade networks, and visual features","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384517","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"While current meeting tools are able to capture key analytics from both text and voice (e.g., meeting summarization), they do not often capture important types of conversations (e.g., a heated discussion resulting in a conflict being resolved). We developed a framework that not only analyzes text and voice, but also quantifies fundamental types of conversations. Upon analyzing 72 hours of conversations from 85 real-world virtual meetings together with their 256 self-reported meeting success scores, we found that our quantification of types of conversations (e.g., social support, conflict resolution) was more predictive of meeting success than traditional voice and text analytics. These new techniques will be essential to uncover patterns in online meetings that might otherwise go unnoticed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhou, Ke","Constantinides, Marios","Aiello, Luca Maria","Joglekar, Sagar","Quercia, Daniele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384718"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nokia Bell Labs"],"keyword":["Meetings","NLP"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of different types of conversations for meeting success","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MPRV.2021.3115879","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384718","identifier":[{"id":"85121687901","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e9f28556-7ad6-4874-9b29-971f3aec6409"],"keyword":["NLP","meetings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9339332773C2FDC70C8C4709C28994A8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MPRV.2021.3115879","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86442289/output.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Ke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marios","key":"constantinidespau","last":"Constantinides","name":"Constantinides, Marios","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","locid":"6aed9698-9a0c-4956-be0d-ec658bbfe09a","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-0654-2527","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sagar","key":"joglekarpau","last":"Joglekar","name":"Joglekar, Sagar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniele","key":"querciapau","last":"Quercia","name":"Quercia, Daniele","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mprv.2021.3115879","issn":["15361268","15582590"],"issn_org":["15361268"],"issue":"4","journal":"IEEE Pervasive Computing","pages":"35-42","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Pervasive Computing","title_org":"I E E E Pervasive Computing","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121687901"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e9f28556-7ad6-4874-9b29-971f3aec6409"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Role of Different Types of Conversations for Meeting Success","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Machine learning and AI-assisted trading have attracted growing interest for the past few years. Here, we use this approach to test the hypothesis that the inefficiency of the cryptocurrency market can be exploited to generate abnormal profits. We analyse daily data for 1, 681 cryptocurrencies for the period between Nov. 2015 and Apr. 2018. We show that simple trading strategies assisted by state-of-the-artmachine learning algorithms outperform standard benchmarks. Our results show that nontrivial, but ultimately simple, algorithmic mechanisms can help anticipate the short-term evolution of the cryptocurrency market.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Alessandretti, Laura","ElBahrawy, Abeer","Aiello, Luca Maria","Baronchelli, Andrea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-321325"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Baronchelli, Andrea"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City, University of London","Nokia Bell Labs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anticipating cryptocurrency prices using machine learning","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/8983590","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-321325","identifier":[{"id":"85057092377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-385c6f1e-a764-4541-bb35-f1a808ab827f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD8B71200512A6DCDC6170F45987EC9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/159260911/8983590.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2018/8983590","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"city university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City, University of London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"nokia bell labs","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Nokia Bell Labs","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura","key":"alessandrettipau","last":"Alessandretti","locid":"0e9909a3-464d-4dbe-8e3a-05327a3bc245","name":"Alessandretti, Laura","orcid":"0000-0001-6003-1165","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Abeer","key":"elbahrawypau","last":"ElBahrawy","name":"ElBahrawy, Abeer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopau","last":"Aiello","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"baronchellipau","last":"Baronchelli","name":"Baronchelli, Andrea","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2018/8983590","issn":["10762787","10990526"],"issn_org":["10762787"],"journal":"Complexity","paperid":"8983590","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Complexity","volume":"2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057092377"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-385c6f1e-a764-4541-bb35-f1a808ab827f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Anticipating Cryptocurrency Prices Using Machine Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-321325","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we investigated the use of tangible widgets vs. the use of finger touch for tablet games, which to our knowledge has not been researched so far. A user test was conducted where participants would report which of the two interaction methods they preferred for playing two tablet games: a fast-paced and a slow-paced game. We conclude that some of the participants found tangible widgets to be an interesting and potentially entertaining interaction method, even though our implementation had technical shortcomings compared to finger touch. Further study is needed to investigate how to fix these shortcomings, and how to increase the game experience of tablet games using tangible widgets.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Mads Bock","Fisker, Martin","Topp, Kasper Steen Fischer","Kraus, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120298"],"event":{"acronym":"SocInfo","end":"2014-11-10","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2014-11-10","title":"First Exploration on Games and Gamers Workshop","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Games","Multi touch","Tablet","User Interface","capacitive screen","finger touch","tangible widget"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"initial exploration of the use of specific tangible widgets for tablet games","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-120298","identifier":[{"id":"84924402389","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f1a0b6eb-3afd-4bc5-9241-c71e55b11de4"],"keyword":["capacitive screen","finger touch","games","multi-touch","tablet","tangible widget","user interface"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8E3E6341633B280EFFDDE357A0A29859"],"oai":